function unit3EvidencePage(){return "<p class=\"eyebrow\">UNIT 3 / CONVENTIONS AND PRACTICAL EVIDENCE</p><h1>Show the skill.</h1><p class=\"lede\">Checked convention guidance and six activities help turn teaching material into observable learner evidence.</p><div class=\"notice\">No learner results are prefilled. Textual pseudocode guidance was checked; network-symbol visual fidelity and actual practical demonstrations remain pending.</div><h2>Pseudocode conventions</h2><p>The current SCSA support booklet gives guidance rather than a single mandatory grammar. Use clear keywords, indentation, explicit block endings, initialisation and an unambiguous distinction between assignment and comparison. Earlier language-neutral algorithms remain explanatory; the clinic supplies convention-focused examples.</p><pre><code>FUNCTION FindID(records, target)\n    low = 0\n    high = records.length - 1\n    middle = 0\n    WHILE low &lt;= high\n        middle = (low + high) DIV 2\n        IF records[middle][0] == target THEN\n            RETURN middle\n        ELSE IF records[middle][0] &lt; target THEN\n            low = middle + 1\n        ELSE\n            high = middle - 1\n        END IF\n    END WHILE\n    RETURN -1\nEND FindID</code></pre><p>Original example: ascending unique IDs; index or -1. Integral midpoint and inclusive candidate bounds are deliberate. Trace empty, one-item, first/last and absent before implementation.</p><h2>Network diagram checks</h2><p>The source’s classroom convention places the perimeter firewall outside the trusted network without requiring an IP label. A router supplies subnet gateways. Earlier combined firewall/router concepts describe possible engineering roles; the formal redraw task separates them. A perimeter firewall alone does not automatically enforce internal inter-zone restrictions.</p><p>Identify the source symbols and compare your legend/diagram visually. The source text was retrieved, but its PDF symbol images could not be rendered here; visual fidelity remains an explicit open check. The pack links the official reference rather than reproducing or certifying generic symbols.</p><h2>Six evidence activities</h2><ol><li>Independent array/dictionary/search/sort pseudocode</li><li>Breakpoint, stepping and focused/regression repair evidence</li><li>Representative workload/environment measurements</li><li>Fresh subnet design and isolated application</li><li>Cisco-convention diagram and policy evaluation</li><li>Authorised live ping/traceroute and limited conclusions</li></ol><p>Embed these in existing practice slots; replace equivalent tasks rather than adding weeks. If only synthetic/paper work is available, retain the appropriate practical status as pending.</p><p><a class=\"button\" href=\"unit3-evidence-pack.zip\" download>Download convention and evidence pack</a> · <a href=\"unit3-evidence-activities.md\" download>Student activities</a> · <a href=\"unit3-evidence-teacher.md\" download>Teacher checkpoints</a> · <a href=\"unit3-evidence-record.csv\" download>Blank evidence record</a> · <a href=\"unit3-conventions-pseudocode.md\" download>Pseudocode clinic</a></p><p>Teacher answers are separate, not access-protected. Retain student records locally; no names/results need to be uploaded. Source: <a href=\"https://senior-secondary.scsa.wa.edu.au/__data/assets/pdf_file/0003/1090875/Year-11_12_Computer-Science_ATAR_Additional-syllabus-support-booklet-.PDF\">SCSA support booklet</a>, <a href=\"https://www.cisco.com/c/en/us/about/brand-center/network-topology-icons.html\">Cisco icons</a> and the <a href=\"#unit3-coverage\">Unit 3 audit</a>.</p>";}
